# Links

Show every link in the link colour, with an underline. Then people can tell a link from the text around it without relying on colour alone.

The words in a link are owned by [Write effective links](../content/writing-guidelines/add-links.html). It explains how to describe the destination and when to say a link leaves Home Assistant or opens a new tab.

## Link states

civica cards draw a link in 3 states:

| State | How it looks |
| --- | --- |
| Default | Link colour, with a thin underline |
| Hover | Link colour, with a thicker 3px underline |
| Keyboard focus | Dark text on the focus colour, with a dark bar under it and no underline |

civica has no visited link colour. A dashboard link usually goes to a screen that changes all the time, such as a room or the energy dashboard, so showing that it was visited does not help.

## Link colour in light and dark mode

Links use `link-color`, which follows the household's theme colour. In dark mode the civica theme switches to a lighter link colour, so links stay readable on a dark card. [Web-app colours](colour-web-app.html#functional-colours) gives both values.

In forced colours mode, such as Windows high contrast, civica action links use the system link colour instead.

## Keep the underline

Keep the underline on a link in a sentence or a list. Do not remove it to make a card look tidier.

A group of [action links](../components/action-links.html) still underlines each name. The arrow beside it is decorative.

## Style a link in a custom card

Use the theme variable, not a fixed colour, so the link follows the theme colour and dark mode.

```css
.link {
  color: var(--link-color);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
}
.link:hover {
  text-decoration-thickness: 3px;
}
.link:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid transparent;
  color: var(--civica-focus-text);
  background: var(--ha-color-focus);
  box-shadow: 0 -2px var(--ha-color-focus), 0 4px var(--primary-text-color);
  text-decoration: none;
}
```

A link goes to another screen. To turn on a light or run a scene, use a [button](../components/buttons.html) instead.
